.TH SAFESHELL 1 "November 2026" "safeshell 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
safeshell \- a safety layer for your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B safeshell
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B safeshell
rates every shell command by how reversible it is (R0 read-only to R4
catastrophic), can run it in a rootless sandbox first to show what it would
change, blocks the dangerous ones with a reason and a safer alternative, and
keeps a snapshot so the last approved command can be undone.
.PP
Run
.B safeshell install
once to add the hook to your shell startup file. After that every command you
press Enter on in bash or zsh is checked first.
.SH COMMANDS
Every command accepts
.B \-h
or
.BR \-\-help ,
which prints its help and does nothing else.
.TP
.BI "check [--json] " command
Rate a command without running it. Exit status 0 means R0 to R2, 3 means R3, 4 means R4.
.TP
.BI "analyze [--json] [--verbose] [--cwd " DIR "] " command
Rate a command, run it in the sandbox, and report the real files, processes and disks it would touch.
.TP
.BI "simulate [--json] [--verbose] [--cwd " DIR "] [--timeout " DURATION "] " command
Run a command in the sandbox and show what it changed. Real files are never touched.
.TP
.BI "explain [--why] " command
Analysis plus a plain-English explanation. Needs an AI model.
With
.B \-\-why
it instead shows which rule and which evidence (ESTIMATED, INSPECTED, PREVIEWED or OBSERVED)
set the final level; this works without an AI, and the explanation is added when one is set.
.TP
.BI ask " request"
Turn a request written in English into a command, which is then checked like any other.
.TP
.B ai setup|status|stop|bench
Manage the optional built-in AI. Nothing is downloaded until you run
.BR "ai setup" .
.TP
.B voice [setup [\-\-yes]|status|\-\-text]
Speak a request. The speech is turned into text on this machine and then handled like
typed English. Run
.B voice setup
once to install the tools it needs (cmake, g++ and a recorder, with apt-get after asking;
.B \-\-yes
skips the question), build the speech engine and download the model.
.TP
.RB "undo [" ID ]
Put back what the last approved command changed, and verify it.
.TP
.B snapshots
List saved snapshots.
.TP
.B daemon [stop]
Keep SafeShell warm in the background for faster checks.
.TP
.B learn [on|off|status]
Learning mode, off by default. When on, each command that passes without a warning gets one line saying what it does, its level and the safer form. It only adds output.
.TP
.B install [--ai], uninstall
Add or remove the shell hook.
.TP
.B hook bash|zsh
Print the shell hook.
.TP
.B doctor
Check every part and say what to fix: sandbox, hook (installed and active in this terminal), daemon, snapshots, AI and cloud key. It only reads.
.TP
.B tour
A one-minute walk-through in a throwaway folder: an R0 command, a blocked rm -rf, a snapshot and an undo. Nothing is left behind.
The hook mentions the tour once per user, in a terminal.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/safeshell/config.json
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/safeshell/keys.json
API keys for cloud models, readable only by you.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/safeshell/audit.jsonl
Log of decisions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAFESHELL_AI
Override the AI mode: auto, off, local, cloud or hybrid.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY ", " GEMINI_API_KEY
Cloud model keys, used instead of the key file.
.SH NOTES
The program is called
.B safeshell
and not
.B ss
because
.BR ss (8),
the socket statistics tool, already uses that name.
.SH AUTHORS
Samarth Vala and Tavish Gupta.
